The Devin/Cascade protobuf sources vendored under crates/adapter-devin/proto
are derived from the widevin project at commit
6c48392052caaecca820ec41df9d87ed818dfc21.  Those sources are distributed
under their upstream MIT license, preserved in
crates/adapter-devin/LICENSE.widevin.  Their provenance is documented in
crates/adapter-devin/NOTICE and fixtures/devin/README.md.

The management dashboard embeds selected Iconoir icons (MIT), LobeHub Icons
(MIT), Simple Icons artwork (CC0-1.0), and Geist and Geist Mono fonts
(OFL-1.1).  It also embeds resized and recoloured Coder Company marks.  The
component versions, source evidence, transformations, asset paths, copyright
notices, and known license texts are recorded under
third-party/dashboard-assets/.  Where the available generation records do not
establish a version, source revision, copyright owner, or license, the manifest
says so rather than inferring one.  Names and logos may be subject to trademark
rights not granted by the listed copyright licenses.

Release archives include machine-readable CycloneDX and SPDX software-bill-of-
materials files under sbom/.  Those files identify the licenses and sources of
the Rust dependencies and the non-Cargo dashboard components embedded in each
archive.  The dashboard asset manifest and known license texts are also shipped
under third-party/dashboard-assets/.
